# Wave 42 §P item 1 — the W18 soft-lock. Match `m-09487f336215`: Relentless
# Dead's second dies trigger ("you may pay {X}. If you do, return another
# target Zombie creature card … from your graveyard to the battlefield",
# `forge-gui/res/cardsfolder/r/relentless_dead.txt`) targets a card in the
# GRAVEYARD — `InputSelectTargets` (a selection, not an `ask`) names an id
# that is on no battlefield, and nothing in the browser could click it.
#
# Seat 0 (human) controls Relentless Dead, four untapped Mountains and one
# untapped Swamp, holds Kozilek's Return (`{2}{R}`, "deals 2 damage to each
# creature" — `k/kozileks_return.txt`), and already has TWO mana-value-1
# Zombie creature cards, Diregraf Ghoul and Dread Wanderer (both `{B}`), in
# its graveyard — a REAL choice between two legal targets, not a lone one.
# Measured against the real jar: with only one Zombie in the graveyard,
# Forge's own trigger-targeting (`TargetSelection`, reached while the
# triggered ability is put on the stack, before it is even offered as a
# `getAbilityToPlay` "play this trigger?" choice) picks the sole legal
# target with NO wire frame at all — no `ask`, no `setSelectables` — so a
# one-target graveyard never exercises the targeting UI and proves nothing
# about it. Two targets forces Forge to actually ask.
#
# Casting Kozilek's Return deals 2 to each creature, which is lethal to
# Relentless Dead's own 2/2 — BOTH its dies triggers go on the stack
# (confirmed against the real jar: each reaches the wire as its own
# `getAbilityToPlay` ask, "which ability to play", one option each). The
# first one to resolve, `TrigReturn` (pay `{B}`, return Relentless Dead to
# hand), needs the Swamp to be payable at all — without it `Auto` never
# enables and the whole stack sits forever, which is a scenario-setup bug,
# not Forge's; this item is not about that trigger. The second, `TrigChange`
# (the one this item is about), has `SVar:X:Targeted$CardManaCost`, so X is
# computed FROM the chosen target — either one's mana value, 1 — meaning the
# TARGET is picked before the cost is even known; one spare Mountain after
# paying `{2}{R}` and `{B}` covers that X whichever target is chosen. Seat 1
# has no creature, so Kozilek's Return's damage never costs it anything
# relevant to this scenario.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=Kozilek's Return
humanbattlefield=Relentless Dead;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Swamp
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=Diregraf Ghoul;Dread Wanderer
aihand=
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
